# API contract

## When to use
- New or changed JSON for `/api/*` consumed by dashboard or external clients
- Align `docs/api-spec.md` with implementation

## Inspect first
- Implementing route file under `backend/src/routes/`
- Consumer: `frontend/app/lib/v3DashboardFetchers.ts` and `app/types/index.ts`
- `docs/api-spec.md`, `backend-go/docs/openapi.yaml` only if Go service must stay in sync (separate stack)

## Steps
1. Document method, path, query params, and example JSON response.
2. Implement backend with stable field names (camelCase in JSON for dashboard DTOs).
3. Add/update TypeScript interfaces on frontend fetchers (source of truth for UI typing).
4. Prefer additive changes (`optional` fields) over renames; if renaming, update all fetch sites in one change.
5. Use HTTP codes: 200 success, 404 missing resource, 403 disabled feature, 500 server error.

## Response patterns in this repo
```json
{ "success": true, "data": { } }
{ "success": false, "error": "message" }
```

## Verification
- [ ] Frontend types match live response (network tab or logged sample)
- [ ] `success: false` handled in fetcher and panel UI
- [ ] `docs/api-spec.md` updated when contract is public/stable
